Patch 0130: a second grid state short of a prompt's end (issue #173). A drafted prompt keeps its
prompt state at floor(n / grid) * grid; on a long prompt that point can sit inside the final turn's
text (the tail question of a fresh request, the last user message of an agent turn), so a later prompt
sharing everything before the tail is no longer a prefix of the kept state and prefills from scratch:
a same-prefix second question paid a full cold prefill above long contexts (misses from ~790k on this
stack), while shorter ones hit. The extra state sits GRID_TAIL (256) tokens earlier, in the shared
prefix, and keeps that request's hit; the end grid state still gives an exact replay its credit.
Same bits: prefill is the same for any chunking, and kept states only choose prefill reuse
(resumed prompts equal fresh ones); the sequential prefill just stops once more.
CPU check: tools/grid_tail_check.py (kept-state lengths for a long prompt with a tail).
